---

# 145. Component Dependency Rule

Components may depend downward:

```text
Domain
 ↓
Composite
 ↓
Primitive
 ↓
Tokens
```

They must not create circular dependencies.

Example:

```text
Button
```

must not depend on:

```text
ProjectWorkspace
```

---

# 146. Domain Isolation

Project-specific components may consume:

- project domain models
- canonical statuses
- domain permissions

Generic components must not import project-specific models.

---

# 147. No Page-Specific Global Components

Do not put one-off page components into the global design system merely for convenience.

A component belongs globally when:

- reused
- semantically stable
- broadly useful
- independently testable

---

# 148. No CSS Escape Hatch Culture

Global component usage should not devolve into:

```text
className="make-it-like-this"
```

for every page.

If a repeated styling need exists, evolve the component/token system.

---

# 149. Component Variants Governance

Variants should represent meaningful semantic differences.

Good:

```text
Button variant="primary"
Button variant="destructive"
```

Bad:

```text
Button variant="greenLargeRoundedShadow"
```

---

# 150. Responsive Governance

Do not create separate desktop and mobile components unless interaction models genuinely differ.

Prefer:

```text
same semantic component
+
responsive composition
```

---

# 151. Accessibility Governance

Accessibility failures in shared components must be treated as system-level defects because one defect can propagate across many pages.

Fix the component once rather than patching dozens of pages.

---

# 152. Visual Governance

If a component visually violates Soft Intelligence:

- do not compensate on every page
- fix the component
- validate against tokens
- update component documentation
- run visual regression

---

